---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The follow-up agent's task, one of two modes: verify a finished run's drafted follow-ups
  and put the verified tickets on the followups board, or answer the board comments one
  gathering quoted.
variables:
  mode:
    description: >-
      Which dispatch this task is for: `initial` verifies the run's drafts and files what
      stands; `feedback` answers the board comments one gathering quoted and nothing else.
      The caller decides it, never the feedback's content; any other value refuses the render.
    type: string
    required: true
  acceptance_criteria:
    description: >-
      Criteria beyond each mode's own, which this template states as fixed items after these;
      empty unless a caller adds one.
    type: list
    items: string
    default: []
  run:
    description: The run whose follow-ups this dispatch works, as `just runs` lists it.
    type: string
    required: true
  board:
    description: The plan source verified tickets are copied onto — `followups`, or the one `--to` named.
    type: string
    required: true
  drafts_root:
    description: The absolute root of the `drafts` plan source the launch exported, which holds the run's drafts and tickets.
    type: string
    required: true
  checkout:
    description: The absolute path of the checkout that launched this dispatch, where every store command is run.
    type: string
    required: true
  plan_store:
    description: The absolute path of this checkout's pinned plan-store program, which every store instruction names in full.
    type: string
    required: true
  validate:
    description: The command that validates one ticket file through the store.
    type: string
    required: true
  board_status:
    description: The command that decides the status a ticket is copied with, and writes its binding and priority estimate.
    type: string
    required: true
  board_items:
    description: The command that answers one narrowing query of a board, every page, as one JSON result.
    type: string
    required: true
  copy:
    description: The command that copies a ticket onto the board item it is bound to.
    type: string
    required: true
  re_estimate:
    description: The command that recomputes one board item's priority estimate from its comments.
    type: string
    required: true
  shape:
    description: >-
      The identifiers and numbers of a ticket's stored shape, as the validators hold them —
      its source, paths, record fields, headings, vocabularies and the exit statuses — so the
      prose names the words the validators read rather than a copy of them.
    type: object
    required: true
  evidence_marker:
    description: The exact last line of this run's evidence comment on another run's issue, with a `<root-cause>` placeholder.
    type: string
    required: true
  evidence_opening:
    description: The visible first line of this run's evidence comment.
    type: string
    required: true
  reply_marker:
    description: The exact last line of this run's reply to a person's comment, with its placeholders.
    type: string
    required: true
  reply_opening:
    description: The visible first line of this run's reply to an attributed comment, with its placeholders.
    type: string
    required: true
  reply_opening_unattributed:
    description: The visible first line of this run's reply to a comment the feedback reports no author for.
    type: string
    required: true
  placement_note:
    description: >-
      The note every direct node of this host carries, saying the dispatch works in the
      launching checkout and commits nothing.
    type: text
    required: true
  feedback:
    description: >-
      The feedback file's text, verbatim: in `feedback` mode the gathering of board comments
      this dispatch answers; in `initial` mode a manager's feedback on the previous follow-up
      run, or no answer when there is none.
    type: text
    required: false
  redispatch:
    description: >-
      Whether an earlier follow-up agent already worked this run, so its tickets, issues and
      comments may already exist. `initial` mode only.
    type: boolean
    default: false
  accepted_statuses:
    description: The accepted board statuses as prose, each as its board option and store word. `initial` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  dispositions:
    description: The path of the disposition account the launch opened for this run's drafts. `initial` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  check_dispositions:
    description: The command that checks the disposition account. `initial` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  ticket_example:
    description: The example ticket, every placeholder in it, as the stored record renders. `initial` mode only.
    type: text
    default: ""
  disposition_example:
    description: The example disposition account, written from the keys its validator reads. `initial` mode only.
    type: text
    default: ""
  budgets:
    description: The path of the budget account the launch measured this run's landed changes into. `initial` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  check_budgets:
    description: The command that checks the budget account. `initial` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  budget_example:
    description: The example budget account, one `over` entry, written from the keys its validator reads. `initial` mode only.
    type: text
    default: ""
  withdrawal:
    description: >-
      The one status change a comment dispatch makes — withdrawing this run's own proposal
      whose ticket a quoted comment, or investigating it, shows is no longer relevant, and
      never a deferred one — in the words the gathering's preamble also carries.
      `feedback` mode only.
    type: text
    default: ""
  responses:
    description: The path of the response account answering the gathering. `feedback` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  check_responses:
    description: The command that checks the response account. `feedback` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  feedback_file:
    description: The gathering's file name, which the response account records. `feedback` mode only.
    type: string
    default: ""
  response_example:
    description: The example response account, written from the keys its validator reads. `feedback` mode only.
    type: text
    default: ""
